    </ol>
  </nav>

  <header class="qa-header">
    <p class="qa-pillar">Question · Biology</p>
    <h1>How Much Does a Raven Weigh?</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="qa-snippet" aria-label="Direct answer">
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> A Common Raven weighs 690–1,630 g (1.5–3.6 lb), with males heavier than females. The range varies by subspecies: birds from cold climates in the High Arctic are the heaviest; those from warmer, southerly regions are lighter. The Thick-billed Raven of the Ethiopian Highlands rivals or exceeds the Common Raven as the heaviest corvid.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Common Raven Weight in Detail</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> The <em>Handbook of the Birds of the World</em> and <em>Birds of the World</em> accounts give the following data for Common Raven (<em>Corvus corax</em>):<sup><a href="#src-1">1</a></sup><sup><a href="#src-2">2</a></sup></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Overall range:</strong> 690–1,630 g (1.5–3.6 lb)</li>
      <li><strong>Typical adult male:</strong> 1,100–1,400 g</li>
      <li><strong>Typical adult female:</strong> 800–1,100 g</li>
      <li><strong>Body length:</strong> 54–67 cm (21–26 in)</li>
      <li><strong>Wingspan:</strong> 115–150 cm (45–59 in)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These are ranges across the full species. Individual birds outside these ranges are possible, particularly very large individuals from the High Arctic subspecies <em>C. c. principalis</em>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Weight Across All Ten Raven Species</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> Weights for each species from published field guides and species accounts:<sup><a href="#src-1">1</a></sup></p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Species</th><th>Weight range</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/common-raven/">Common Raven</a></td><td>690–1,630 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/thick-billed-raven/">Thick-billed Raven</a></td><td>c. 1,000–1,500 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/white-necked-raven/">White-necked Raven</a></td><td>c. 440–780 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/chihuahuan-raven/">Chihuahuan Raven</a></td><td>c. 400–600 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/australian-raven/">Australian Raven</a></td><td>c. 650–900 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/forest-raven/">Forest Raven</a></td><td>c. 650–900 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/little-raven/">Little Raven</a></td><td>c. 310–430 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/fan-tailed-raven/">Fan-tailed Raven</a></td><td>c. 350–540 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/brown-necked-raven/">Brown-necked Raven</a></td><td>c. 400–600 g</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/species/somali-crow/">Somali Crow</a></td><td>c. 350–500 g (limited data)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Note: data quality varies considerably. Common Raven and Australian Raven have large sample sizes; Fan-tailed Raven, Forest Raven, and Somali Crow have fewer published measurements. Treat values for less-studied species as approximate.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Why Does Raven Weight Vary?</h2>
    <p><strong class="claim-science">[science]</strong> Several factors drive the weight variation seen within and between raven species:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Bergmann's Rule:</strong> birds (and other endotherms) tend to be larger at higher latitudes and altitudes, where conserving body heat is an advantage. High Arctic Common Ravens are the largest in the species; desert populations are smaller.</li>
      <li><strong>Sex:</strong> males are heavier than females by 10–15% in most species (sexual size dimorphism).</li>
      <li><strong>Season and condition:</strong> pre-breeding adults in poor habitats may weigh less than the published minimum; well-fed birds in autumn may exceed the typical maximum.</li>
      <li><strong>Subspecies:</strong> the 11–12 subspecies of Common Raven vary substantially in size.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="qa-section">
    <h2>Related Questions</h2>
